WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.870
Guess who might be looking to put on his happy
face again, bringing a little laughter and

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.870
a lot of anarchy to the mean streets of Gotham?

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:12.369
In the eight decades since making his appearance
in the pages of Batman #1, he's been called

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.500
everything from "The Clown Prince of Crime,
to "The Ace of Knaves," to "Puddin'."

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:19.680
"You know what's great about you, Puddin'?

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.680
You really put the 'fun' in 'funeral.'’

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.800
He's also been called a psychopath who "just
wants to watch the world burn."

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.500
Todd Phillips and Joaquin Phoenix are calling
him Arthur Fleck, though most of us have come

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.310
to know him simply as Joker.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:40.960
By the end of director Phillips and star Phoenix's
new film, Joker, that's presumably the name

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:42.840
and villainous persona Arthur will take.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:47.860
While the pair's anxiously anticipated film
is still weeks away from release, it's already

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:51.760
generating a whirlwind of mostly positive
press on the festival circuit — with many

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.580
critics praising Phoenix's turn as the titular
baddie as the best incarnation of the Joker

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:57.120
yet.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:02.400
Some are even speculating Phoenix's performance
may well net him the Best Actor statue that's

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.670
somehow eluded the actor throughout his diverse
and ambitious career.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:10.610
Understandably, that sort of praise already
has people buzzing about whether or not there's

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:15.040
a chance for a Joker 2, and whether or not
Phoenix would be open to reprising his role

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:15.580
for it.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.260
So, will we ever see a Joker sequel?

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:19.480
Let's discuss.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:24.160
Joker was pitched and produced as a standalone
project, so we can tell you right off the

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.920
bat that there is no immediate plan for a
Joker follow-up.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:32.440
That being said, director Todd Phillips recently
went on the record with Total Film to state

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:36.620
he would be more than willing to make another
Joker movie if Phoenix were on board for the

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:41.570
project — and he certainly makes it sound
like Phoenix might be considering the possibility.

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:42.729
He told Total Film:

00:01:42.729 --> 00:01:46.680
"One thing I will tell you: I would do anything
with Joaquin, any day of the week.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:48.440
There's nobody like him.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:52.840
If he was willing to do it, and if people
show up to this movie, and Warners came to

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.350
us and said, 'You know what?

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:55.830
If you guys could think of something…'

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:59.320
Well, I have a feeling that he and I could
think of something pretty cool."

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:04.010
There's a lot to unpack in that quote, so
before we get too ahead of ourselves, we can

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:08.590
tell you that Phoenix himself has neither
confirmed nor denied his interest in appearing

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:12.670
in a Joker sequel — but what's interesting
about Phillips' statement is how clear it

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:16.840
is that both he and Phoenix had a ton of fun
bringing their version of Joker to life.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:21.920
Furthermore, if one were inclined toward a
bit of conjecture, you could also take Phillips'

00:02:21.939 --> 00:02:25.999
comment as a hint that the two have already
thought of where they'd take the story, and

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.239
are just waiting to see how Joker plays with
audiences before pursuing the next step.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:31.520
"'How's your job?

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.300
Are you having any negative thoughts?'

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:39.080
All I have are negative thoughts."

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:43.599
For Phillips' part, he's seemingly already
brought a game-changing concept to the fray

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:44.860
for this first Joker.

00:02:45.269 --> 00:02:49.340
As has been well covered in the press, this
incarnation of the Joker is a version of the

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:52.700
character that has nothing to do with any
Joker that's appeared before.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:57.880
Free from the shackles of comic book lore,
TV, and cinematic canon, Phillips and Phoenix

00:02:57.889 --> 00:03:01.809
set out to make the most of their blank slate
and craft a version of Joker the likes of

00:03:01.809 --> 00:03:03.220
which have never been seen before.

00:03:03.909 --> 00:03:07.900
As for whether or not Phoenix will return
for a Joker sequel, we'll just have to wait

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:08.440
and see.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:12.620
Robert Pattinson certainly stoked the fires
of rumor-ville by inadvertently alluding to

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:17.680
a possible cameo of Phoenix's Joker in his
upcoming The Batman, but Phoenix has been

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.740
quite vocal about the emotional toll the role
took on him.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:25.920
He told reporters during a Venice Film Festival
presser that while playing Joker, you, quote,

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:26.900
"start to go a little mad."

00:03:27.609 --> 00:03:31.860
Even if the studio wants a sequel, the idea
that Phoenix would return to the role doesn't

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:32.860
seem guaranteed.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:37.840
While it may be a challenge for Phoenix to
step back into the makeup for Joker 2, Phillips'

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:42.409
remarks also imply that Joker's box office
take and critical reception may well influence

00:03:42.409 --> 00:03:43.560
whether or not it happens.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:48.419
Critics are already being very kind to the
film — but the rest, as it seems, is up

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.420
to the moviegoing public.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:54.440
If you want to see Phoenix and Phillips return
for Joker 2, make sure you show Joker a little

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.800
love when the film finally arrives in theaters
on October 4.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:03.580
"When you bring me out… could you introduce
me as 'Joker?'"

